---
import DocShell from '../layouts/doc-shell.astro';
import { docsLinks } from '../lib/nav';
import checkVerbose from '../samples/check-verbose.txt?raw';
import assessment from '../samples/relevance-assessment.json.txt?raw';

const toc = [
   { id: 'what', label: 'What relevance is' },
   { id: 'signals', label: 'What a1 looks for' },
   { id: 'states', label: 'The four states' },
   { id: 'see', label: 'See why a criterion is listed' },
   { id: 'limits', label: 'Limits' },
];
---

<DocShell
   title="Relevant criteria"
   summary="<p>Not every criterion applies to every page. A page with no form has no form errors to test. <code>a1 check</code> looks at what a page is made of and lists the criteria worth checking on it.</p>"
   links={docsLinks}
   toc={toc}
>
   <section>
      <h2 id="what">What relevance is</h2>
      <p>
         The <strong>Check by hand</strong> list in <code>a1 check</code> is the set of
         criteria that are relevant to the page and that a scan cannot decide. It is a
         checklist cut down to this page.
      </p>
      <p>
         Relevant means worth checking. It does not mean failing, and it does not mean
         passing.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="signals">What a1 looks for</h2>
      <p>
         a1 reads the page as the browser rendered it and records signals in 15 categories.
      </p>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt>Structure</dt>
         <dd><code>heading</code>, <code>landmark</code>, <code>media</code>, <code>help</code></dd>
         <dt>Widgets</dt>
         <dd><code>dialog</code>, <code>menu</code>, <code>overlay</code>, <code>tablist</code>, <code>widget</code>, <code>drag-and-drop</code></dd>
         <dt>Forms and updates</dt>
         <dd><code>form</code>, <code>repeated-form</code>, <code>validation</code>, <code>live-region</code>, <code>auth</code></dd>
      </dl>
      <p>
         Each WCAG criterion has topic tags from the W3C, such as <code>forms</code> or
         <code>navigation</code>. When a signal matches a criterion's tags, the criterion is
         relevant.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="states">The four states</h2>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt><code>relevant</code></dt>
         <dd>The page has something this criterion is about. Check it. The text report says "yes".</dd>
         <dt><code>not-detected</code></dt>
         <dd>a1 found nothing this criterion is about. The text report says "not seen".</dd>
         <dt><code>out-of-scope</code></dt>
         <dd>The criterion does not apply to this kind of content.</dd>
         <dt><code>unknown</code></dt>
         <dd>The signals were not enough to say.</dd>
      </dl>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="see">See why a criterion is listed</h2>
      <p><code>a1 check --verbose</code> adds a table of every criterion.</p>
      <pre data-label="OUTPUT"><code>{checkVerbose.trimEnd()}</code></pre>
      <dl class="defs">
         <dt>Scanner checks</dt>
         <dd>What axe found for the criterion: failed, passed, or no rule.</dd>
         <dt>Applies here</dt>
         <dd><code>yes</code> for relevant, <code>not seen</code> for not-detected.</dd>
         <dt>How to check</dt>
         <dd>The <a href="/test-methods">test method</a>: a scan and a person, or a person.</dd>
      </dl>
      <p>
         A row can read <code>✓ passed</code> and still need a person. The scan passed the
         part it covers.
      </p>
      <p><code>--json</code> has the detail in three places.</p>
      <dl class="defs defs--wide">
         <dt><code>result.relevance.signals</code></dt>
         <dd>Each signal, with the elements that produced it.</dd>
         <dt><code>result.relevance.matrix.assessments</code></dt>
         <dd>Each relevant criterion and the reason it is relevant.</dd>
         <dt><code>result.criteria</code></dt>
         <dd>One row for every criterion, relevant or not: the scan's verdict, the relevance state, and the test method.</dd>
      </dl>
      <pre data-label="OUTPUT"><code>{assessment.trimEnd()}</code></pre>
      <p>
         This is the fixed <a href="/guides/demo">practice page</a>. Its confirmation message
         is a <code>role="status"</code> element, which is a live region, so 4.1.3 Status
         Messages is relevant. On the broken page there is no live region, and 4.1.3 is
         <code>not-detected</code>. The broken page fails the criterion and a1 does not list
         it. That is the main limit.
      </p>
   </section>

   <section>
      <h2 id="limits">Limits</h2>
      <dl class="defs defs--wide">
         <dt>Something missing leaves no signal</dt>
         <dd>A status message with no live region, or a custom control with no role, gives a1 nothing to detect. <code>not-detected</code> is not a pass.</dd>
         <dt>The match is broad</dt>
         <dd>Tags are general, so a1 can list a criterion that does not apply to the page. You decide that when you check it.</dd>
         <dt>Only what is on the page counts</dt>
         <dd>A dialog that is added after a click is not there yet. To open it first, use <code>--click &lt;selector&gt;</code>.</dd>
         <dt>An audit does not skip criteria</dt>
         <dd><a href="/guides/audit"><code>a1 audit</code></a> decides every criterion in scope on every page. Relevance is a hint for development, not a way to drop work from an audit.</dd>
      </dl>
   </section>
</DocShell>
